  "contract": "Design capital upgrades plus a four-period repeating tap schedule. Preserve source network, loads, ratings, source voltages and fixed conventional generators. Demand growth 1.30 multiplies original P and Q; profile generation multipliers apply only to sgen. Approved corridor upgrades install THREE total identical parallel circuits; transformer_parallel means identical parallel units in each original bank. All original banks receive the same approved tap in each six-hour period; positive HV-side ratio tap lowers LV voltage. Tap choices are the common original device catalogue; networks without tap changers allow only zero. Daily cyclic sum of absolute tap changes must be <=18, a declared experimental operating limit. Each scenario is four quasi-static AC power flows; no electromagnetic transient or storage dynamics are modelled. Outage removes one installed circuit or transformer only during its declared periods. Unserved buses, nonconvergence, voltage outside 0.95-1.05 pu or line/transformer loading over 100% fail. No load shedding, renewable curtailment or artificial rating/source changes. This is a finite experimental contract, not full N-1 or field certification. A transformer outage removes ONE unit from the declared transformer_bank only, not one unit from every bank.",
  "difficulty_stratum": "coupled_design"
}
